\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Rises For 5th Session But RBI Caps;Bonds Dn\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2009\par 15:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      As Of 1200 GMT \par                      Latest      Change \par    USD/INR           47.11       -0.27 \par    6.05% 2019 Bond   6.48%       +5 BPs \par    Call Rate         3.10%       -40 BPs \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    April             1.105       0.035 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is the midpoint of bid-offer spreads \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose for the fifth consecutive session and hit a six-month high during the day as the dollar weakened globally and strong capital inflows poured in.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it has done all this week to prevent a sharp rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR47.11, down from INR47.38 at the previous close. It touched INR46.98 early in the session, a level last seen Nov. 5.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is said to have lifted the greenback from this lowpoint up to INR47.20 before exporters and foreign banks stepped in to sell again.\par \par \uc2 Market participants said that a clutch of exporters, who were long of the dollar, are now selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cash in on post-election euphoria.\par \par \uc2 "We're seeing some flows via the recent qualified institutional placements but most of the selling is coming from unwinding of long dollar positions ahead of anticipated further capital inflows. We see the dollar continue to remain under pressure," said R.V.S. Sridhar, senior vice president of treasury at \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some, however, say that the rupee's rise could be overdone.\par \par \uc2 "With the kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  we have seen from the RBI and the recent sharp run-up, these levels look attractive to buy the dollar now," said a foreign bank's dealer.\par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, prices were pressured by a heavy supply of debt from a INR150 billion bond auction.\par \par \uc2 The 6.05% 2019 bond ended at INR96.90, down from INR97.29 Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Prices, though, recovered slightly as the cutoff yield at the auction was lower than expected. However, a foreign bank bond dealer said the supply overhang will continue to keep buyers on the back foot.\par \par \uc2 He said he expected the 10-year yield to range between 6.45% and 6.55% next week.\par \par \uc2 -By Bijou George; Dow Jones Newswires +91 22 61456116; bijou.george@dowjones.com [ 22-05-09 1307GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090522e55m000i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
