\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE:RBI's Gopinath:No Change In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Policy\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 03:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (This article was originally published Tuesday) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Anant Vijay Kala & Subhadip Sircar \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed its policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will continue to curb volatility, \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Shyamala Gopinath\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We are closely monitoring the situation," Gopinath said on the sidelines of an event, when asked about the recent sharp fall in the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The comments come on a day when the rupee hit a fresh all-time low, breaching INR52 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has lost 6.2% against the dollar so far this year on top of a 19% fall in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has sold net $31.7 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the rupee's fall in the current fiscal year till December.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the RBI's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been intermittent even as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has posted sharp falls over the past several sessions.\par \par \uc2 "As we know the dollar has strengthened against other majors. Our policy on the rupee has not changed," Gopinath said.\par \par \uc2 She said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will ensure that the government's bond market borrowing program is conducted in a smooth manner.\par \par \uc2 "RBI as a debt manager to the government would ensure that we conduct the borrowing in a smooth and non disruptive way," Gopinath said.\par \par \uc2 The government has upped its borrowing program four times this fiscal year to INR3.06 trillion from the INR1.45 trillion originally budgeted in February 2008.\par \par \uc2 It plans to borrow INR3.62 trillion in the next fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 The RBI is conducting open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy back bonds and also buying back market stabilization scheme bonds, issued earlier to cushion the market from supply concerns by ensuring comfortable liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "All I can say is that we monitor all developments closely and take actions as appropriate, necessary," Gopinath said when asked about the possibility of further interest rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts are widely expecting the RBI to slash rates after economic growth was at its slowest pace in nearly six years during October-December.\par \par \uc2 The economy expanded 5.3% during the period under review, compared with 7.6% during the July-September quarter.\par \par \uc2 Last Friday RBI Governor Duvvuri Subbarao met banks chiefs and asked them to lower lending and deposit rates.\par \par \uc2 "Banks have to take their (interest rate) decisions based on their asset and liability profiles. It is a commercial decision but yes we have seen them starting to respond," Gopinath said.\par \par \uc2 India's largest state-run lender \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  Monday slashed the interest rates it offers on some deposits by 40-50 basis points.\par \par \uc2 -By Anant Vijay Kala & Subhadip Sircar, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 03, 2009 21:59 ET (02:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090821e5340m0u6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pn