\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank says sells $318 mln in December\b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2009\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $318 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December, sharply lower than $3.1 billion it sold in November, as the rupee pulled back from a slide.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India sold $2.323 billion in December and bought $2.005 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed, taking the total net sales to $11.42 billion in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee recovered 2.9 percent in December, but still closed 2008 down 19.1 percent on the year as foreign funds pulled more than $13 billion from the domestic share market in the wake of the global financial turmoil.\par \par \uc2 In 2007, record portfolio inflows of $17.4 billion had helped the rupee rise more than 12 percent.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen sharply to $251.53 billion in early February from a peak of $316 billion last May, partly reflecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 By 4:37 p.m. (1107 GMT) on Tuesday, the rupee was trading at 49.50/51 per dollar after hitting 49.66, its lowest since Dec. 8. It has fallen 1.6 percent so far this year as foreigners withdrew about $1 billion since the start of January. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokum