\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank says sells net $3.1 bln in November\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2009\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 14 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $3.1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November, sharply lower than $18.67 billion it sold in October, to help slow down a falling rupee.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> fell more than 21 percent between January and November as foreign funds pulled out from the stock market in the wake of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India sold $5.456 billion in November and bought $2.355 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed on Wednesday, taking total net sales to $11.1 billion in the first 11 months of 2008.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> fell more than 21 percent between January and November as foreign funds pulled out from the stock market in the wake of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners have withdrawn about $310 million from Indian shares in 2009, after dumping more than $13 billion last year.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen sharply to $255.24 billion in early January, after hitting a peak of $316 billion in May last year, partly reflecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the rupee ended at 48.85/86 per dollar, down 0.3 percent this month.\par \par \uc2 In 2008, the rupee fell 19 percent, after gaining more than 12 percent in 2007 when foreigners bought a record $17.4 billion of stocks. (Reporting by V. Ramakrishnan; Editing b