\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Hits Record Low, Bounces On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ;Bonds Up\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2008\par 14:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           50.15      -0.13 \par  8.24% 2018 Bond   7.00%      -6 BP \par  Call Rate         6.15%      Unchanged \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  November          0.950      +0.020 \par  \par *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and a sharp recovery in local shares helped the Indian rupee end higher Tuesday, staging a smart recovery from an all-time low hit during the session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR50.15, down from INR50.28 in the previous session. Earlier, it rose to INR50.58, breaching the previous record of INR50.57 posted Nov. 20.\par \par \uc2 "The rupee has been tracking the global markets of late. I see no short-term respite for it if the global economic problems continue to worsen by the day," said a dealer with a state-run bank. He expects the greenback to test INR51 by next week.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , in a research note, said it expects the dollar to be at INR50.50 in three months, INR48.00 in six months and INR46.90 in 12 months.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to remain weak in the near-term due to portfolio outflows, and as corporates as well as banks swap rupees for dollars to meet their credit and funding needs, Goldman said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee was initially dragged lower as confirmation that the U.S. slipped into a recession in Dec. 2007 and weak manufacturing data from U.S. and China pushed local stock markets down.\par \par \uc2 However, local shares clawed back late in the session on short covering, helping the rupee post late gains.\par \par \uc2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's benchmark 30-stock Sensitive Index, or Sensex, ended down 1.1% at 8739.24. The index fell as much as 4.2% to 8,467.43 in early trade, hurt by the sharp overnight fall on Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, Indian government bond prices rose on increasing risk aversion as recessionary fears continued to haunt global markets.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds also drew strength from crude oil prices, which settled at $49.28 per barrel on the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2  Monday, the lowest in three and a half years.\par \par \uc2 The 8.24% bond due 2018 ended at INR108.39, up from INR108.00 in the earlier session. The yield on the note fell 6 basis points to 7.00%.\par \par \uc2 "Global economies and equity markets are in turmoil. These are healthy times for bonds as markets hope for more rate cuts," said a dealer with a local bank.\par \par \uc2 However, concerns of fresh bond supplies on speculation that the federal government may announce its excess borrowing plan for the current fiscal year prompted traders to take profits.\par \par \uc2 "Traders may take profits, but sooner or later we will see the yield fall below the 7.00% mark convincingly as global interest rates continue to trend downwards," said the head of bond trading at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Anant Vijay Kala; Dow Jones Newswires +91 22 22884212-18; anant.kala@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-12-08 1318GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081202e4c2000ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
