\par\par \b \uc2 Indian cbank says sells net $3.8 bln in September\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2008\par 14:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 12 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $3.8 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, when the rupee dropped past the 47 per dollar level to its weakest in more than 5 years.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 sold $6.48 billion in September and bought $2.7 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In August, it bought $3.8 billion and sold $2.6 billion, while in July the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $9.9 billion, the highest in a month since the RBI began publishing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures in April 1995, and bought $3.58 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought a net $10.67 billion between January and August, the monthly RBI bulletin showed.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell more than 16 percent in the first nine months of 2008, ending September at 46.95/96 per dollar <INR=IN>. Last month, it hit a record low of 50.29 on heavy foreign withdrawals from a slumping stock market.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the rupee ended at 49.30/32, down 20 percent this year. In 2007, record portfolio inflows of $17.4 billion had helped the rupee rise to a near decade high of 39.16 in November.\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds are net sellers of $12.7 billion this year. (Reporting by Anurag Joshi, Editing by Mark Williams)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/ \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081112e4bc001dy\par }\page {\par\f