\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Indian Bankers Say Liquidity Remains A Concern\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2008\par 08:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2 , finance ministry.)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Insufficient liquidity in India is a concern as external credit lines dry up, and the government needs to take proactive steps to ensure that the banking system remains flush with cash, bankers said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Liquidity is a major issue but as far as I know authorities are aware of it and they will continue to provide positive bias towards liquidity from now into the future," O.P. Bhatt, chairman of \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY) said at a banking conference.\par \par \uc2 With the financial crisis making global credit scarce, Indian corporates are increasingly looking to local banks for funds to meet their requirements.\par \par \uc2 "Liquidity is also required to continue to meet the (shortfall) in the future as many of the lines of credit that were available globally are not available," said Chanda Kochhar, joint managing director and chief financial officer at ICICI Bank (532174.BY).\par \par \uc2 Overnight rates in India's interbank market shot up to the 21% level last week on a cash squeeze stemming mainly from heavy rupee-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a host of measures Saturday to cool lending rates, including a cut in the repo rate by 50 basis points as well as a 100 basis point cut in the cash reserve ratio and statutory liquidity ratio.\par \par \uc2 Call rates have subsequently eased to around 6%-7% levels.\par \par \uc2 A senior Finance Ministry official Thursday said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves have been successful.\par \par \uc2 "Call money rates have come down. It is a sign of success. Money is accessible. My sense is that the call money rate will continue to be calm," the executive, who didn't want to be named, said in New Delhi.\par \par \uc2 Banks Haven't Asked For Dollar Loans Yet\par \par \uc2 Bankers said that they haven't approached the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet for dollar-denominated lines of credit for their overseas branches. "We are not asking for dollar loans and we are not asking it for capitalization," said Bhatt.\par \par \uc2 ICICI Bank's Kochhar also said that ICICI hasn't made such a request to the RBI.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the government official said that India is currently not facing a shortage of dollars in its cash market.\par \par \uc2 "The last set of announcements has addressed the dollar liquidity issue. My personal sense is that it (dollar liquidity crunch) is behind us," the official said.\par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar, Harsh Joshi, John Satish Kumar & Mukesh Jagota; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 06-11-08 0752GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081106e4b6000iw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
