\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hits record low, cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2008\par 05:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold $2 bln to lift rupee off low\par \par \uc2 * Losses in local stocks heighten worries of capital outflows (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 22 (Reuters) - The rupee slumped to an all-time low on Wednesday before trimming losses on heavy dollar sales by state-run banks, but a slide in the stock market indicated there would be more pressure on the Indian unit.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 49.28/29 per dollar, 0.5 percent weaker than Tuesday's close of 49.04/06. It hit a record trough of 49.50, at which point it was down 20.4 percent in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee would have fallen more had the state-run banks not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They are likely to have sold nearly $2 billion today," said Agam Gupta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Standard Chartered Bank. "If they had not we would have been at 50 already."\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to smoothen the heavy demand for dollars, but was not trying to defend any particular level.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward rupee contracts <PNDF> were at 50.79/94, nearly 3 percent weaker than the onshore spot rate, indicating a bearish outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares fell 4.8 percent in a broad-based selloff, erasing the previous sessions gains, as recession fears hammered international equity markets. [.BO]\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have sold a net $12.2 billion worth of Indian shares this year, and the stock market is down by half in 2008. Last year, the funds had bought a record net $17.4 billion, and the stock market rose 47 percent.\par \par \uc2 A stronger dollar overseas was also hurting rupee sentiment, dealers said. The dollar soared to a two-year high against the euro and a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a worsening global economic outlook prompted more investors to liquidate risky assets in favour of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [USD/] (Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081025e4am0001n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
