\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee weaker on stocks, cbank seen supporting\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2008\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee falls sharply as stock losses weigh\par \par \uc2 * Traders say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after early fall\par \par \uc2 * Crude refiners buy dollars for import payments (Updates to mid-session)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell sharply on Wednesday as a fall in share prices triggered worries of an accelerated outflow of foreign funds, but traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off its lows.\par \par \uc2 At 12:31 p.m. (0701 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 48.445/45 per dollar, 0.8 percent lower than Tuesday's close of 48.04/06. It hit an all-time low of 49.3 last week.\par \par \uc2 "FIIs are selling in this market and this has turned the sentiment on rupee shaky," a trader with a state-run bank said, referring to foreign institutional investors.\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have sold a net $11 billion of Indian shares this year, including $1.7 billion this month.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars through state-run banks after the rupee had fallen to 48.62 in early deals.\par \par \uc2 The main share index <.BSESN> fell more than 4 percent, weighed down by tight cash conditions, which the rupee-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exacerbates, and worries about the risk of a global recession.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said dollar demand from oil firms also put downward pressure on the rupee. Oil <CLc1> is India's biggest import, and refiners are the largest buyers of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. (Reporting by Anurag Joshi; Editing by John Mair)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081018e4af0004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
