\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia mostly down ahead of US bailout vote\b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2008\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended losses on Wednesday, pressured by the dollar's broad strength ahead of a U.S. vote on a revised version of the $700 billion package to bail out the troubled financial sector.\par \par \uc2  But trading was thinned by holidays in Indonesia, the Philippines, China and Malaysia.\par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=TH> fell 0.4 percent to 33.98 against the dollar as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported by hopes that U.S. lawmakers could still reach a deal on the bailout plan days after an original plan was rejected. [ID:nSP361078]\par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar surged sharply against its major rivals as investors shifted their focus to spill over from U.S. financial crisis to other countries," said a trader in Bangkok.\par \par \uc2  The U.S. Senate will vote on Wednesday night on a new version of the $700 billion bailout package for Wall Street, reviving hopes that the credit crisis can be stemmed before causing further damage to the global economy. [ID:nSP54674]\par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee <INR=IN> dipped to a fresh five-year low at 47.23 per dollar amid fears of capital outflows, but the loss was limited by official warnings about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as usual, Shyamala Gopinath, deputy governor at the Reserve Bank of India said on Wednesday. [ID:nBOM69927]\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell to 32.232 to the U.S. dollar as foreign banks bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it was off a eight-month low at 32.368 hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> bucked the region's weakness, gaining 1.9 percent to 1,184.9 per dollar on hopes of the passage of U.S. bailout plans and official pledges to support the won.\par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Bae Kook-hwan said the country would take steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the won moved too sharply. [ID:nSEO344865]\par \par \uc2  Vishnu Varathan, economist at Forecast, said in a note that he expected the won to fall past the 1,200 level in the coming months the Bank of Korea may have to cut interest rates in response to falling inflation.\par \par \uc2  Data issued on Wednesday showed South Korean's inflation fell to 5.1 percent in September from 5.6 percent in August and 5.9 percent in July, which was the biggest annual rise in 10 years.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a squeeze in dollar funding persisted.\par \par \uc2  The rate on overnight dollar funds <USDOND=> hovered near 6 percent in Singapore and Thailand compared to as high as 8 percent on Tuesday after U.S. lawmakers unexpectedly rejected a $700 billion vote to bail out the financial sector.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rate shot up to 10 percent earlier this month when \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 ' collapse sparked a resurgence in the year-old global credit crisis.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0528 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.89         106.03       +0.13\par  Sing dlr        1.4352         1.4335       -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      32.064         32.130       +0.21\par  Korean won     1190.50        1207.00       +1.39\par  Baht             33.95          33.85       -0.29\par  Rupee            47.06       