\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India MOF Exec: Expect RBI To Hold Rates Steady\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gaurav Raghuvanshi   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2008\par 13:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--India's federal finance ministry expects the Reserve Bank of India to hold key policy rates steady at its Oct. 24 meeting, a senior ministry official said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "There is little scope for cuts in the cash reserve ratio and the statutory liquidity ratio now," the official, who asked not to be named, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Under SLR, Indian banks must invest at least 25% of their deposits in gold, cash and government securities, ensuring a captive market for sovereign debt. India's cash reserve ratio, or the proportion of deposits banks have to set aside as cash with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is 9%. "There is a liquidity problem currently, but the situation will improve once the government pays INR250 billion to banks under the farm loan waiver," the official said.\par \par \uc2 The Indian government had earlier said it will waive off INR670 billion in small farm loans, and banks will be compensated in cash over the next three years.\par \par \uc2 The official said the government plans to pay interest to commercial banks on the amount of farm loans that they have already waived off under a government program to boost fresh lending to the agriculture sector.\par \par \uc2 The first chunk of the loans were waived off on June 30.\par \par \uc2 On the sharp decline in the value of the Indian rupee against the dollar in recent weeks, he said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to check volatility.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI doesn't target any level for the rupee. Their clear policy on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to check volatility," he said.\par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the year, the rupee has lost nearly 16% against the dollar, erasing gains of over 12% last year.\par \par \uc2 The rupee touched an over five-year low of INR47.23 to a dollar in early trade on Wednesday, but later recovered on suspected RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 1110 GMT, the dollar was changing hands at INR46.69.\par \par \uc2 The official also said the current global financial crisis is likely to slow India's movement toward fuller capital account convertibility as suggested by a government-appointed panel that set a roadmap for easing capital controls last year.\par \par \uc2 "You can't keep moving at the same pace if things are happening around you," he said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91-11-4356-3300; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-10-08 1152GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081001e4a1000k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
