\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Fall Sharply As Auction Demand Seen Poor;Rupee Dn\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2008\par 16:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           46.55      +0.23 \par  8.24% 2018 Bond   8.59%      +2 BPs \par  Call Rate         8.50%      -150 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  September         0.49       -0.14 \par  \par *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices slumped after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  required primary dealers to support a bond auction, suggesting poor demand for the securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 And there was more bad news to come for the market. After trading hours, the federal government announced its borrowing calendar for the second half of the year, front-loading the entire half-yearly borrowing calendar to October to December. Dealers said the move raised concerns of a sharp overshoot in the government's annual borrowing plan.\par \par \uc2 The 8.24% 2018-dated bond ended at INR97.73, down from INR97.87 in the previous session. Its yield rose two basis points to 8.59%. The benchmark note had earlier reached an intraday high of INR98.87.\par \par \uc2 "Though the market had been fearing it, it is quite well understood now that the government will have to borrow substantially more than their initial plans," said a senior bond dealer at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 The dealer said the auction had come as a setback to the market as the government was forced to cut back due to low-priced bids.\par \par \uc2 "It had happened at the state auctions yesterday also. Big banks did not participate in the auction today as demand for SLR's (Statutory Liquidity Ratio) has come down significantly while the bond tenors were unattractive," the dealer added.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India sold INR60 billion of 7.94% 2021 bonds and INR40 billion of 8.28% 2032 bonds. The cutoff yield on the 2021 paper came in at 9.0369%, well above the 8.95% median forecast of a Dow Jones poll of five market participants. The cutoff yield on the 2032 paper was at 9.2628%, also above the poll estimate of 9.17%.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, bonds rose as crude oil prices fell, while traders drove up demand ahead of the quarter-end for corporate results.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market was set for a sharply lower opening Monday as trade resumes after the borrowing plan announcement and liquidity squeezes again due to the auction outflows.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee fell against the U.S. dollar, hurt by strong demand for the greenback from oil companies to pay for monthly imports.\par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR46.55 Friday, up from INR46.22 in the earlier session.\par \par \uc2 "There was heavy demand from a few large oil firms which were unable to buy earlier because of the strike by state-run banks," said a dealer at a private bank.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also drew strength from sharply weaker local shares, dragged down by weak Asian peers and uncertainty surrounding the proposed $700 billion U.S. bailout package.\par \par \uc2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's 30-stock Sensitive Index, or Sensex, closed down 3.3% at 13,102.18.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to ease the rupee's slide, selling the dollar from near its intraday high of INR46.58.\par \par \uc2 -By Anant Vijay Kala; Dow Jones Newswires +91 22 22884212-18; anant.kala@dowjones.com [ 26-09-08 1420GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080926e49q000pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
