\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank sold $9.9 bln in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  market in July\b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2008\par 14:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 12 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a gross $9.9 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July, the highest on record, in a volatile month when the rupee hit a 15-month low but then later rose 1.1 percent on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $6.32 billion on a net basis in July, trimming its net dollar purchases in 2008 to $13.24 billion.\par \par \uc2 The $9.9 billion gross is the most sold in a month by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 since it began publishing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures in April 1995. It surpasses record dollar sales of almost $7 billion gross in June.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell 7.4 percent in the first seven months of 2008, ending July at 42.57/58 per dollar <INR=IN>, in a reversal of its fortunes in 2007 when strong foreign investment inflows drove it to 39.16, its highest in nearly a decade.\par \par \uc2 This year's fall accelerated sharply in July as crude touched a record above $147 a barrel, the trade deficit widened, and investment outflows weighed.\par \par \uc2 Traders say that in recent months and days the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to support the rupee, which is now at its lowest in two years, has shed nearly 4 percent this month alone and lost 13.9 percent this year. (Reporting by Anurag Joshi; Editing by Charlotte Cooper)\par \par \b \