\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Eyes on S.Korea as Asian c.banks defend  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2008\par 04:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates levels, adds Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 2 (Reuters) - Central banks in Malaysia, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  and elsewhere in Asia defended their weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, but analysts suspected that South Korea's hands-off stance may deter others from standing firmly in the way of their falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said it had sold dollars to put a floor under the baht <THB=TH>, which hit a one-year low of 34.49 per dollar on growing political tensions.\par \par \uc2  Thai Prime Minister Samak Sundaravej declared a state of emergency in Bangkok on Tuesday and gave the army control of public order after overnight clashes between pro- and anti-government protesters.\par \par \uc2  Market participants also reported \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Malaysia, the Philippines and Indonesia as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  there buckled under the U.S. dollar's broad rally, the latter hitting an 8-month high against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as oil prices fell.\par \par \uc2  "All central banks are trying their best to stop the flood of outflows," a trader in Singapore said.\par \par \uc2  In South Korea, where the won <KRW=> has been plumbing multi-year lows, the authorities restricted their efforts to meetings, warnings. Dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if any, was light as the volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a new 4-year low near 1,134 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  No one is sure why the Korean authorities have loosened their grip and let the won weaken, but market participants believe it is either because they want to shore up exports or out of reluctance to spend reserves against an inevitable dollar rally.\par \par \uc2  Analysts said Korea's indifference to won weakness could weaken the resolve of other central banks.\par \par \uc2  "It's very difficult if one goes, particularly if it's a large and important third-markets competitor for the rest of the region, like Korea," said Simon Flint, a strategist at \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 . "It becomes difficult for the others to resist depreciation from a trade-weighted perspective.\par \par \uc2  "Secondly, it weakens people's belief in the ability of the central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  effectively once they have seen one \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't do as they have apparently said they will do."\par \par \uc2  INDIA ALSO STEPS IN\par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of India was also spotted selling dollars but the rupee <INR=IN> still continued falling to hit a new 1-\u189\'00\'BD   year low of 44.35 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold dollars at 3.4190 and 3.4180 per dollar, a trader in Kuala Lumpur said, but the ringgit persisted with its decline.\par \par \uc2  The rupiah <IDR=> hit a low of 9,196 per dollar, its weakest since Aug. 19. A trader in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars from 9,190.\par \par \uc2  "It's not large. I think they realise that there is no point \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in a dollar bull market all over the place," said one trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2  In the Philippines, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling dollars as the peso <PHP=> reached 46.60 per dollar, its weakest in almost a year.  (Reporting by Vidya Ranganathan; Editing by Jan Dahinten)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA/CENTRALBANKS (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|SNI|PHD|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080902e4920002w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
