\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected as  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee avoids 43/dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 By Swati Bhat   \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2008\par 08:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, June 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was propped up by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, traders said, first just avoiding 43 per dollar and then strengthening despite the stock market dropping after inflation topped 11 percent.\par \par \uc2  The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 42.93/94, off a low of 42.99 and 0.1 percent stronger than Thursday's close of 42.97/98, even as the stock market slumped to a 10-month low.\par \par \uc2  "There was a lot of corporate demand in the market today, and once that was over, the (state) banks selling dollars started putting pressure on the dollar-rupee," said Paresh Nayar, chief dealer at \uc2 Development Credit Bank.\par \par \uc2  One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts <PNDF> were at 43.21/31, 0.64 percent weaker than the onshore rate.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee hit a 13-month low of 43.21 per dollar last month, and since then traders say it has been acting to keep the rupee stronger than 43 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  Data showed India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves declined by $5 billion in the week to June 13, which analysts say partly reflects dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the rupee.\par \par \uc2  Inflation shot above 11 percent in early June to a 13-year high following a rise in state-set fuel prices, rattling markets and prompting the finance minister to warn of stronger anti-inflation measures ahead. See [ID:nDEL287411]\par \par \uc2  Dealers said the higher-than-expected inflation hurt sentiment on the rupee, as it reduces its purchasing power. It also sent the main share index <.BSESN> to its low for 2008.\par \par \uc2  The stock index is down more than 28 percent this year, which has been a factor in the rupee's 8 percent-plus fall against the dollar.\par \par \uc2  Foreigners have sold a net $5.9 billion worth of shares so far this year. In 2007, they bought a record net $17.4 billion of stocks, helping push the rupee up by more than 12 percent.  (Editing by John Mair)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080623e46k000d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
