\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:Dlr Rises Vs India Rupee To Over 1Yr High On Oil Bids\b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2008\par 07:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  (Adds background, more analysts comments, latest level) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar rose to an over one-year high against the Indian rupee Thursday as oil refining companies bought the greenback in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, spooked by surging global crude oil prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The rupee, the second best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2007, is currently in a tailspin as foreign investment in local equities has slowed to a trickle, and analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get weaker in the near term.\par \par \uc2 "High oil prices and inflation are not supportive of a stronger rupee in the near term," said Craig Chan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Lehman Brothers.\uc2  He expects dollar to trade at INR43.50 by the end of May.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has lost 8.6% of its value against the dollar so far in 2008.\par \par \uc2 At 0505 GMT, the dollar was changing hands at INR43.15, after touching an intraday high of INR43.20. It was last this high on April 9, 2007, when it traded at INR43.06.\par \par \uc2 "Unless there is a sharp jolt to the market - a sudden weakening of dollar globally or some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - I suppose we'll see INR43.50 level in the near term," said Sundeep Bhandari, managing director and head of global markets, South Asia, at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \par \uc2 India imports nearly two-thirds of its total oil needs and the spurt in global crude oil prices is widening its trade deficit.\par \par \uc2 "We have to remember that the current account deficit of countries like India and Korea will weigh much more on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  than others in Asia," he added.\par \par \uc2 The country's trade deficit was $80.4 billion in the fiscal year that ended March 31.\par \par \uc2 "I don't expect the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively as the rupee is now nearing its equilibrium value. They may step in to control any panic reactions, though," said Rupa Rege Nitsure, chief economist at \uc2 Bank of Baroda.\par \par \uc2 - By Harsh Joshi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; harsh.joshi@dowjones.com [ 22-05-08 0513GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080522e45m000lt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
