\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Pushed To Near 1-Yr Low By Higher Oil;Bonds Down\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2008\par 14:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           41.77       +0.41 \par  8.24% 2018 Bond   7.88%       +1 BPs \par  Call Rate*        6.00%       +25 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  March             0.57        -0.04 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount, Call Rate, Mifor and OIS rates are midpoints of bid-offer spreads. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee slid further against the dollar Thursday, falling to its lowest level in nearly a year as oil refining companies led a broad-based dollar buying spree in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar strengthened to INR41.77, from INR41.36 at Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 "The market will probably consolidate a bit here, but in the short- to medium-term, we need the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give a signal for a sentiment change or supply some dollars, otherwise the mood will be very bearish (for the rupee)," said \uc2 Agam\uc2  Gupta, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \par \uc2 A surge in global crude oil prices to record highs has led to a dip in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rupee has lost around 3% over the last week.\par \par \uc2 But experts say that possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will catch any further sharp fall in the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There is still some more room for correction (in the rupee), but I don't see much downside from here," said A.V. Rajwade, an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  consultant.\par \par \uc2 "The oil marketing companies have taken a bad hit with such a sudden, sharp fall in the rupee. Somewhere down the line, the need to limit those losses will also weigh on the finance ministry and the RBI," Rajwade said.\par \par \uc2 Trade in the government bond market was cautious as participants consolidated positions ahead of Friday's bond auction.\par \par \uc2 Buying interest also fell victim to renewed concerns over inflation, amid soaring fuel prices.\par \par \uc2 "The market was quite subdued today. Going ahead, I think we need some definite cues, especially how inflation pans out," a dealer at a state-owned bank said.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.24% 2018-dated paper ended at INR102.44, as against INR102.50 Wednesday. Its yield rose 1 basis points to 7.88%.\par \par \uc2 The RBI will sell INR100 billion of government bonds Friday.\par \par \uc2 India's wholesale price index-based inflation rate, due Friday, is expected to be 7.67% on the year according to a Dow Jones Newswires poll, up from 7.57% a week ago.\par \par \uc2 -By Harsh Joshi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; harsh.joshi@dowjones.com [ 08-05-08 1228GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080508e4580011v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
