\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia loses ground; Singapore dlr, ringgit hit lows\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao and Melissa Chia   \par \uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2008\par 06:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Friday against the broadly stronger dollar, buoyed by positive U.S. labour market data and receding expectations of more Federal Reserve interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> retreated from a decade high scaled on Wednesday and the Singapore dollar came off its record high hit on the same day as investors bought the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> fell almost 0.8 percent to 1.3640 to the U.S. dollar, which firmed against the euro and the yen after data released on Thursday suggested the U.S. labour market held up well despite slumping home values. [ID:nN24402636]\par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar gained extra headway against the euro after soft German business sentiment data cast doubt on the outlook for the euro area economy. [ID:nBEB002074]\par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar is moving in line along with the euro, while the Malaysian ringgit is also getting slightly sold down," a trader in Singapore said.\par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar took a long time breaking 1.3590, and there are a lot of investors selling at 1.3600," said the trader.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaked at an all-time high of 1.3468 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> fell as far as 3.16 per dollar, down about 0.5 percent to its lowest level in more than a week.\par \par \uc2  Markets still factor in a moderate 25 basis point cut in U.S. interest rates next week, but many investors believe the Fed is ready to take a break after that. Futures markets are now pricing in a 30 percent chance that the Fed will keep its benchmark unchanged at 2.25 percent at its upcoming policy meeting.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Thai baht <THB=TH> touched a two-week low at 31.66 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  Thai finance minister Surapong Suebwonglee said on Friday that the authorities did not target any particular baht rate against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2  "Our principle is that we will like to have the Thai baht move in line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2  The baht, one of Asia's top performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has gained about 6.5 percent against the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2  BEARISH ON RUPEE\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> fell 0.3 percent to 42.1 per dollar, as concerns about mounting global and local inflationary pressures dampened investor confidence.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates steady on Thursday, but warned it would jack up rates if commodity-fuelled inflation spread to the broad economy.\par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee <INR=IN> fell to a one-month low at 40.25 per dollar, weighed by dollar buying by oil firms and other importers and fears of a possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "In our view, deteriorating current account dynamics, muted portfolio inflows and presence of the RBI's bid will lead to further rupee weakness," analysts at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2  "Separately, we recommend investors stay paid \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards as valuations are still attractive and as the RBI will increasingly rely on forwards to sterilise rupee liquidity," they added.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  expects the rupee to fall to 41 to the dollar by the end of June.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0812 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.64         103.82       -0.78\par  Sing dlr        1.3637         1.3535       -0.75\par  Taiwan dlr      30.335         30.297       -0.13\par  Korean won      994.00         995.75       +0.18\par  Baht             31.65          31.56       -0.28\par  Peso             41.97          41.98       +0.01\par  Rupiah         9225.00        9218.00       -0.08\par  Rupee            40.19          40.17       -0.05\par  Ringgit         3.1580         3.1430       -0.47\par  Yuan            7.0090         6.9970       -0.17\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.64         111.33       +6.39\par  Sing dlr        1.3637         1.4382       +5.46\par  Taiwan dlr      30.335         32.443       +6.95\par  Korean won      994.00         935.70       -5.87\par  Baht             31.65          33.68       +6.41\par  Peso             41.97          41.28       -1.64\par  Rupiah         9225.00        9390.00       +1.79\par  Rupee            40.19          39.41       -1.94\par  Ringgit         3.1580         3.3050       +4.65\par  Yuan            7.0090         7.3041       +4.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080428e44p000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
