\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Govt Bonds Gain On Good Liquidity; Rupee Up On Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2008\par 14:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           40.12       -0.06 \par  8.24% 2018 Bond   8.15%       -3 BPs \par  Call Rate         6.05%       +80 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  March             0.83        +0.08 \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bonds prices rose Friday, boosted by domestic headline inflation which came in in line with the market's expectations, dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 8.24% 2018-dated bond ended at INR100.58, compared with INR100.39 at its previous close. Its yield fell 3 basis points to 8.15%.\par \par \uc2 "The inflation numbers were somewhat factored in by the market. Still, most of the run was in the new benchmark paper which is seeing good buying interest," said a local dealer.\par \par \uc2 "The liquidity has been good so far, helped by government spending and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wholesale price index-based inflation rate was 7.33% on the year for the week ended April 12, in line with the average of a Dow Jones Newswires poll of 5 economists, which pegged the rate at 7.34%. The inflation rate was 7.14% a week earlier.\par \par \uc2 "There has been a structural shift in the prices across the board. Even with the recent fiscal and monetary measures, we think inflation will stay around 7% till June," said Shubhada Rao, chief economist at Yes Bank.\par \par \uc2 Bond trading was cautious and the volumes were below average as market participants wait for the Reserve Bank of India to reveal its policy stance.\par \par \uc2 The RBI will meet Tuesday to review annual monetary policy for this fiscal year. It is widely expected to hold rates steady to avoid stifling the country's economic growth. It will also probably wait to see the effect of a recent hike in the banks' cash reserve ratio.\par \par \uc2 But a section of the market is still betting on further monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee recouped some of the previous session's losses Friday, helped by a buoyant local stock market.\par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR40.12, as against INR40.18 at its previous close.\par \par \uc2 "But banks will avoid building large positions either way until the RBI takes a decision on the interest rates," the chief dealer at a private bank said.\par \par \uc2 -By Harsh Joshi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; harsh.joshi@dowjones.com [ 25-04-08 1231GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080425e44p000sw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
