\par\par \b \uc2 India inflation moderate in coming months-ministry   \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2008\par 07:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, Feb 28 (Reuters) - Inflation in India should remain moderate in the coming months due to policy measures taken over the last year, the finance ministry said in its annual economic survey on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Rising incomes, rising commodity prices, and dealing with large capital flows were some of the challenges to be faced in keeping prices under check, the 2007/08 economic survey said.   \par \par \uc2 "The behaviour of agricultural prices, including essential consumption items, will be critical, given falling poverty and rapidly rising per capita income," it said.   \par \par \uc2 Supply-side pressures were likely in areas such as the farm sector and infrastructure, and monetary policy needed to address inflationary expectations caused by price rises that were due to supply and demand mismatches, the survey said.   \par \par \uc2 The ministry survey said containing inflation was a priority, because rising prices hurt the poor, and putting pressure on interest rates hit both savings and investment.   \par \par \uc2 Annual wholesale price inflation <INWPI=ECI> hit a six-month high of 4.35 percent in early February, although it was still below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of close to 5 percent for 2007/08.   \par \par \uc2 The government said monetary policy had to juggle continued capital flows and their impact on the exchange rate, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and market liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought almost $75 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2007 trying to contain the rise of the rupee. Such dollar buying adds rupees to the domestic money market, which could be inflationary if left in the system.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised banks' reserve requirement by 250 basis points since December 2006, with the last increase in November, to manage the amount of cash in the banking system. It has also sold special bonds to absorb funds released by its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 For in depth coverage of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  budget 2008 click on:   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://in.reuters.com/news/globalcoverage/indiaeconomy2008"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://in.reuters.com/news/globalcoverage/indiaeconomy2008  }}}\uc2  (Reporting by V. Ramakrishnan; Editing by John Mair)   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-ECONOMY/PRICES (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080228e42s000dl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
