\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises on capital inflow hopes   \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2008\par 04:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The rupee rose on Wednesday on hopes for another U.S. rate cut, which could attract foreign capital to \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited the gains. The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.78/79 per dollar, stronger than Tuesday's close of 39.905/915. During early trade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hit 39.70, its strongest since Feb. 18.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee fell to a five-month low of 40.25 last week.   \par \par \uc2 "Today, we saw the rupee up on the back of the weak dollar," said a senior trader with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar sank to a record low against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, after a U.S. Federal Reserve official on Tuesday suggested interest rates may soon be cut again to fend off a recession in the world's largest economy. See [ID:nL27168912]   \par \par \uc2 The weakening dollar triggered a rally in commodities, with crude, India's largest import, continuing to hover above $101 per barrel.   \par \par \uc2 "We didn't see any big inflows from foreign institutional investors today, but sentiment was up due to equities," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 India's benchmark share index <.BSESN> ended 0.11 percent higher, shedding early gains of nearly 2 percent, as investors sold shares on news European stock indices had slipped into the red. See [ID:nBOM20600]   \par \par \uc2 Inflows of overseas capital are a key driver of the local unit, causing it to climb 12 percent against the dollar in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners bought a net $1.3 billion of Indian equities so far this month, after selling about $4.3 billion in January.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has left its key lending rate steady at 7.75 percent for nearly a year, but in January the Fed slashed its federal funds rate by 125 basis points to 3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Another U.S. rate cut would widen the interest rate differential between the two countries, increasing the flow of foreign funds into higher yielding Indian assets.   \par \par \uc2 "Also, we saw corporates liquidating long dollar positions," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  once the rupee hit 39.73 largely staved off further gains, the dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 "For tomorrow, a lot depends on how the dollar does overnight," the trader said. "But I think we'll be seeing a range of 39.70-39.85," he said. (Reporting by Catherine Bosley; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/(UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080301e42r0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
