\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee up on inflow hopes, cbank hand seen   \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2008\par 10:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee strengthened on Friday on expectations of capital inflows after the U.S. Federal Reserve's rate cuts, but traders said the gains were checked by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.35/36 per dollar, slightly weaker than the day's high of 39.33, its highest since Jan. 21, according to Reuters data.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee ended at 39.38/39 on Thursday and hit a near-decade high of 39.16 percent in November.   \par \par \uc2 Trading volumes for the day were low at $861 million, data provided by Clearing Corporation of India showed.   \par \par \uc2 "It's been a very dull day, not much trading," said Rohan Lasrado, head of trading at  \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Mumbai.   \par \par \uc2 "We've seen capital outflows due to the Reliance (Power) IPO, but these have been offset by capital inflows thanks to the dollar losing ground," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds were net sellers of $841.6 billion on Thursday, taking total sales to about $4.8 billion in the last 12 sessions, after pouring $17.4 billion into Indian equities in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 The main share index <.BSESN> snapped a four-day fall and rebounded more than 3 percent on Friday. See [ID:nBOM40048].   \par \par \uc2 Traders expect demand for local assets to gather momentum in the near term, as a result of the Fed's recent rate cuts.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut rates by a hefty half percentage point on Wednesday, in an attempt to halt a sharp slowdown in the United States.   \par \par \uc2 Flows of foreign capital into India have been a key driver of the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) limited its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, permitting the rupee to gain slightly, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to check the rupee's rise to ensure Indian exports remain competitive.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to the level we anticipated, so we've seen a bit of appreciation," Lasrado added.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080204e421000sk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
