\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Bonds Down Ahead Of Ctrl Bk Review; INR Up On Inflows   \b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2008\par 13:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.37      -0.11 \par  7.99% 2017 Bond   7.42%      +4 BPs \par  Call Rate         6.10%      -180 BPs .Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par .   December        0.67       +0.06 \par *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices ended down Friday in lower-than-average volume as participants booked profits ahead of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy review next Tuesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The 7.99% 2017 bond ended at INR103.80, down from INR104.07 at Thursday's close. Its yield rose to 7.42%, up four percentage points from its previous close.   \par \par \uc2 "The market will remain thin on Monday, too, and we should see some readjusting of positions before the policy. But, on the whole, the market remains positive and expects some reduction in the rates," said Jayesh Mehta, head of debt markets at DSP Merril Lynch.   \par \par \uc2 Bond yields touched two-year lows earlier in the week, as some investors upped the odds of a rate cut by the Reserve Bank of India as uncertainty over the health of the global economy increases and the difference between local and U.S. money-market rates widen.   \par \par \uc2 However, other market participants think the RBI may just hold rates steady as latent inflationary pressures persist and money supply remains high.   \par \par \uc2 "If the fuel prices are revised upwards in the near future, there exists a huge possibility of inflation rate touching 5% by the end of the fiscal year," said Namrata Padhye, fixed-income research analyst at IDBI Gilts.   \par \par \uc2 India's wholesale price index-based inflation rate rose 3.83% on year for the week ended Jan. 12, slightly up from 3.79% the week before. The RBI estimates inflation to be around 5% in the current financial year that began Apr. 1, 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Friday, attendance at trading desks was thin due to a strike by workers at state-run banks who were protesting against mergers among state-owned banks and the outsourcing of business services.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India said Friday it bought INR4.90 billion of bonds in the secondary market in the week ended Jan. 18, down from INR12.30 billion in the previous week.   \par \par \uc2 It sold INR900 million of bonds in the same week, compared with no sales the previous week.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee rose against the dollar, as rejuvenated local stocks brought hopes of more foreign funds into \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the RBI likely capped its gains.   \par \par \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange's 30-stock Sensitive Index, the Sensex, moved 1,139.92 points higher Friday - its highest intraday gain in terms of points - to close at 18361.66, up 6.6%.   \par \par \uc2 "The Indian economy, considering the speed at which it is growing, is going to remain a good investment opportunity for western countries for some time to come," Padhye of IDBI Gilts said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR39.37 Friday, down from INR39.46 at its previous close.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI is believed to have supported the dollar regularly in the past three sessions, though the support level seems to be shifting progressively lower.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by $3.169 billion to $284.898 billion in the week ended Jan. 18, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Friday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Harsh Joshi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; harsh.joshi@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 25-01-08 1232GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080125e41p000ua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
