\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee gains but cbank may block rise   \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2008\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose on Thursday, lifted by gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets after a large U.S. rate cut this week, but the market is worried about the outlook for capital flows in the near term.   \par \par \uc2  At 9:35 a.m. (0405 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 39.50/51 per dollar, stronger than Wednesday's close of 39.58/59 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2  "The flow outlook is still uncertain," said Ajith Dayanand, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at  \uc2 State Bank of Travancore\uc2 , although exporters were selling dollars on any rupee fall.   \par \par \uc2  Over the five sessions to Tuesday foreigners sold $2.6 billion of shares as the share market, caught in a global rout of equities, fell more than 17 percent, before a 75 basis point cut in U.S. interest rates helped steady markets.   \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds bought a record $17.4 billion of shares in 2007, a key driver of the rupee's 12 percent rise in 2007.   \par \par \uc2  The market was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked the rupee off its highs on Tuesday, and was also factoring in a rate cut at a monetary policy review next week.   \par \par \uc2  "Given the 75 basis points Fed cut, the probability of the RBI cutting rates on Jan 29 goes up significantly,"  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said in a note.   \par \par \uc2  Many analysts now expect a 25 basis points rate cut in Indian rates as the premium over U.S. rates has widened to 425 basis points, its widest in more than three years.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $72.1 billion in the first 11 months of 2007 and dealers said it has been active since then in trying to keep the rupee lower.  (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee; Editing by John Mair)     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080127e41o00023\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
