\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-India cbank -- US slowdown a policy factor   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anurag Joshi   \par \uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2008\par 08:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with details, quotes)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The risk of a U.S. recession will be an important consideration at next week's policy meeting of India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the global outlook is now more uncertain than a month ago, the bank's governor said on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Speculation of a rate cut at the January 29 review has increased on the back of expectations of another U.S. rate reduction. Although many analysts are still uncertain, a cut would be the first in more than three years.   \par \par \uc2 "I think we will pay considerable attention to that subject and the monetary policy statement will take note of it," Governor Yaga Venugopal Reddy told reporters in Mumbai when asked if the possibility of a U.S. recession would be a factor in the Indian policy decision.   \par \par \uc2 Last month, Reddy had said the December rate cut by the U.S Federal Reserve was a relevant but not determining factor in Indian monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the governor said the turbulence in global financial markets as a result of the U.S. subprime crisis had been greater than expected.   \par \par \uc2 "On a very preliminary basis, I should say these financial global uncertainties were not entirely unanticipated," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "The intensity was somewhat not predicted nor was the duration. So the outlook seems far more uncertain for global situation than before," Reddy said.   \par \par \uc2 Indian bond yields eased towards their lowest in a year on Monday as stocks tumbled, giving rise to expectations of a near-term rate cut. The 10-year bond <IN079917G=CC> ended at 7.54 percent, slightly above a one-year low of 7.51 percent hit earlier this month.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept its main short-term lending rate on hold at 7.75 percent for nearly 10 months, after raising it five times between between June 2006 and March 2007, 3.5 percentage points above the U.S. federal funds rate of 4.25 percent.   \par \par \uc2 If the U.S. Federal Reserve cuts rates by 50 basis points as widely expected at its meeting on Jan. 29-30, it could boost capital flows to higher-yielding assets in India and pressure the rupee to rise.   \par \par \uc2 Still, analysts say Reddy may sit tight for the time being.   \par \par \uc2 "My sense at this stage is that he will probably stay on hold this time but going forward he might go in for an interim cut," said Abheek Barua, chief economist at  \uc2 HDFC Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Growth concerns will get much emphasis than in the past," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout 2007 as the rupee rose 12 percent against the dollar and traders say it has been active this year trying to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hitting 10-year highs.   \par \par \uc2 Low inflation offers some room for an interest rate cut, although the government is considering raising state-set retail fuel prices and food prices remain a concern.   \par \par \uc2 Reddy said high food and oil prices would continue to shape inflationary expectations.   \par \par \uc2 "Almost for more than a year, we had been very sensitive to that and we will continue to be sensitive to that. Particularly because these are essential commodities which have a very great impact on inflation expectations," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Annual wholesale price inflation was at 3.79 percent at the beginning of January, below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 5 percent by the end of March. (Writing by V. Ramakrishnan; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|SNS|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080121e41l000i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
