\par\par \b \uc2 Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says bought $7.83 bln in Nov   \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2008\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $7.83 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November, when the rupee tested a near-decade high of 39.16 versus the dollar, data showed on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India has been buying dollars heavily to slow down the rupee, which climbed more than 12 percent in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 It had bought $12.54 billion in October, the biggest single-month purchase ever. Total purchases in the first 11 months of 2007 now stand at $72.13 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was lower than in the previous month due to festival holidays in November and as the U.S. subprime crisis roiled global markets, limiting inflows.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign portfolio flows of $17.4 billion into stocks and about $2.3 billion into debt in 2007 have put upward pressure on the rupee, but foreign funds were net sellers of more than $800 million of stocks in November.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> traded in a broad 39.16-39.90 band in November and was the second best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia during 2007 after the Philippine peso.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has picked up since the start of 2008 on flows into new share offerings. A $3 billion initial public offer by Reliance Power was fully subscribed in a minute of its opening on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped $98 billion in 2007 to a record of $275.559 billion on Dec. 28. (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080116e41g0012z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
