\par\par \b \uc2 Cbank holds Indian rupee as inflows rise -dealers   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anurag Joshi   \par \uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2008\par 13:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Jan 14 (Reuters) - The rupee was barely changed on Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the session buying dollars to stem a rise in the Indian unit, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.28/29 per dollar, little changed from the previous close of 39.28/285 and not far from a decade-high of 39.16 hit in November.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI was seen protecting the dollar around 39.2825. It tried to weaken the rupee, but the foreign inflows remained strong," a trader with a state-run bank said, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue this week, traders said, on expected flows into an initial public offering by Reliance Power that opens on Tuesday to raise up to $3 billion in India's largest-ever IPO.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds could pump in about $1 billion for the IPO, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had blocked the rupee from climbing beyond 39.20 last week, and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought an estimated $3 billion so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed last month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $64.3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 10 months of 2007, including a record $12.5 billion in October.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also concerned that firmer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Chinese yuan touching a new high against the dollar, could put upward pressure on the rupee. (Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080117e41e001id\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
