\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee edges up on capital inflow hopes   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee   \par \uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2007\par 04:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee crept up in thin year-end dealing on Wednesday as firmer shares sparked hopes that foreign funds may resume their strong buying of local stocks.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> tiptoed up to end at 39.42/43 per dollar, above Monday's close of 39.45/46. Markets were closed on Tuesday for Christmas.   \par \par \uc2 "It has been a very quiet session ... and dollar-rupee has been in a very narrow range. I expect volumes to pick up at the turn of the year," said V. Kumar, chief dealer at  \uc2 State Bank of Travancore.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares rose 1.7 percent on Wednesday to their highest close in two weeks, powered by index heavyweight  \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  and supported by short covering a day before the expiry of monthly futures contracts. See [ID:nBOM269736].   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds bought about $42 million worth of shares on Monday after selling stocks valued at nearly $1.3 billion in four sessions last week, trimming their net exposure to about $16 billion in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Capital inflows have been a key driver of a stock rally and have helped fuel the rupee's 12 percent rise this year to become the second-best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia against the dollar after the Philippine peso <PHP=>.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying at 39.38-39.40 levels to inject rupee funds into a cash-starved banking system helped keep the local unit in a tight range.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $64.5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 10 months of the year and is widely seen as having played an active role in the rupee market in November and December.   \par \par \uc2 As most dealing rooms are operating with skeleton staffing due to the holidays and with many foreign banks having closed their books for the year, activity was likely to wind down further into the year-end, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  expects the rupee to rise to 37 per dollar by end-2008, supported by strong inflows and less \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check inflation-fuelling cash in circulation.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Mark Williams)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071229e3cq0001l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
