\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee climbs as stocks gain; cbank eyed   \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2007\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose against the dollar on Monday as hefty gains in local stocks cheered sentiment and raised expectations of more capital inflows in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> rose to 39.45/46 per dollar, stronger than Thursday's close of 39.54/55 and moving within sight of a near-decade high of 39.16 hit last month.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were closed on Friday for a holiday and will close again on Tuesday for Christmas.   \par \par \uc2 "Activity has been very thin and the rupee's move is reflective of the stock rise," said R.A. Sankara Narayanan, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at state-run Bank of India.   \par \par \uc2 Indian stocks rose 3.61 percent on Monday to their highest close in more than a week, led by ICICI Bank and  \uc2 Infosys Technologies\uc2  as fears of a U.S. recession eased and the chances declined of early national elections. See [ID:nBOM151816].   \par \par \uc2 Most dealing rooms are operating on a skeletal staff due to the holidays and with many foreign banks having closed their books for the year, activity is likely to wind down further as the year-end nears, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has rallied by about 12 percent against the dollar this year to be among Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Foreign inflows into local stocks have been a key driver of the rupee, but investors have turned sellers recently.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed foreign funds sold a net $1.15 billion of shares in the first three days of last week, after pouring in $1.5 billion in 11 prior sessions.   \par \par \uc2 But analysts said the local unit's gains are expected to be tempered by usual dollar-demand from oil refiners to meet monthly and year-end needs and likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  imports a majority of its oil requirements.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee; Editing by Mark Williams)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071227e3co0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
