\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee climbs on capital inflows; cbank seen   \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2007\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed to its highest close in nearly a month on Friday, driven by strong capital inflows into the fast-growing economy, though sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited gains, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.34/35 per dollar, its strongest finish since Nov. 19, and up from the previous close of 39.395/405.   \par \par \uc2 It hit 39.16 last month, its strongest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "There were strong flows from a single bank today, which put a lot of upward pressure on the rupee," said a dealer with a state bank. "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was there to see that the rupee did not appreciate too fast."   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record $12.544 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October to slow down a rising rupee, which has gained about 12 percent this year, data showed on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $64.5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first ten months of the year and is widely seen as having played an active role in the rupee market in November and December too.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to allow greater flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but will also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee stable, Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan said on Thursday. See: [ID:nBOM72221].   \par \par \uc2 With capital inflows likely to remain steady at best, no significant appreciation was likely in the near term, and the market should be content trading in a range until some decisive cues spur a breakout, dealers said.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by C.J. Kurrien, Editing by Mark Williams)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071217e3ce00050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
