\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee dips on waning flows, cbank concerns   \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2007\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased a touch on Friday, with the market constrained by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the prospect of waning foreign investment flows toward the end of the year, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:40 (0410 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 39.40/41 per dollar, dipping from the previous close of 39.395/405. It hit 39.16 last month, its strongest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "There's talk in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try and push the dollar-rupee rate higher," said a dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "If you kick a running dog, its bound to go further," the dealer added, referring to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the local unit lower.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to allow greater flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but will also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee stable, Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan said on Thursday. See: [ID:nBOM72221].   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $52 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first nine months of the year and is widely seen as having played an active role in the rupee market in October and November too.   \par \par \uc2 With capital inflows likely to be steady at best, no significant appreciation was likely in the near term, and the market should be content trading a range till some decisive cues spur a breakout, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The mood was watchful after the main share index <.BSESN> fell 1.3 percent on Thursday as fresh global credit concerns weighed, after the market climbed to a record high for a third successive day.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by C.J. Kurrien; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071217e3ce0004z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
