\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee caught between inflows, cbank fears   \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2007\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was in a tight range on Thursday with the market caught between possibilities of foreign buying in the record-setting stock market, and the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At 9:40 a.m. (0410 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 39.36/37, a shade higher than the previous close of 39.375/385. It hit 39.16 last month, its strongest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "It's going to be a rangish market till we get some solid cues, and the stock market is one of them," said a dealer with a public sector bank.   \par \par \uc2 The main share index <.BSESN> hit a record high for the second day on Wednesday, and dealers expect the rally to continue, though weak Asian markets may cap gains.   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought Indian shares worth $1.1 billion in the eight days to Tuesday, taking the total purchases since the start of January to $16.9 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign buying of Indian shares has been a key driver of the rupee this year, helping it gain nearly 12.5 percent, to be among Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Still, gains were limited as the dollar hovered near one-month highs against the yen <JPY=> as the U.S. Federal Reserve and other central banks announced measures to ease the credit crunch and support financial firms struggling to secure funds before the year-end.   \par \par \uc2 The prospect of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the local unit, further weighed on sentiment, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $52 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first nine months of the year and is widely seen as having played an active role in the rupee market in October and November too.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by C.J. Kurrien; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071216e3cd0003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
