\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee climbs on inflow hopes ahead of Fed meet   \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2007\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee headed back towards a near-decade high on Tuesday, with investors ratcheting up purchases of the local unit anticipating a burst of capital inflows if the U.S. Federal Reserve cuts rates as expected.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.35/36, per dollar, its highest close in three weeks, and strengthening from the previous close of 39.40/41.   \par \par \uc2 It hit 39.16 last month, it's highest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "The rupee would have gone higher had it not been for the RBI," said a dealer with a corporate, referring to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was widely suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the local unit through the session to temper its rise.   \par \par \uc2 The Fed is expected to lower the key federal funds rate by 25 basis points to 4.25 percent on Tuesday. It has lowered rates twice since mid-September. The decision is expected at 1915 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Sentiment on the rupee was bolstered after India's benchmark share index <.BSESN> surged to a new life high buoyed by investors' expectations of a U.S. rate cut.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a one-month high against the yen and firmed against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in choppy trading ahead of the Fed decision.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the rupee's rise was limited by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which capped the local unit's gains at 39.35.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $52 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first nine months of the year and is widely seen as having played an active role in the rupee market in October and November too.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by C.J. Kurrien; Editing by Mark Williams)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071214e3cb000h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
