\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Bonds Dn On Cash Woes; Rupee Dn On Likely  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2007\par 13:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.41      +0.02 \par  7.99% 2017 Bond   7.88%      +1 BP \par  Call Rate         7.80%      +330 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  November          0.47       Unchanged \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices ended slightly lower Monday, with traders trimming holdings on expectations that short-term cash will get expensive as companies make advance tax payments later this week, market participants said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.99% 2017-dated bond ended at INR100.71, down from its previous close of INR100.78. Its yield rose by one basis point to 7.88%.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the market to trade in a narrow range this week on lingering worries about liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The overnight call money rate rose to 7.80% from its close of 4.50% Friday, another sign that spare funds in the system may start to dry up.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is preparing for the advance tax outflows, while the supply of securities is also expected to tighten cash further," said Manoj Kumar Swain, head of fixed-income trading at Standard Chartered Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Quarterly tax payments by Indian companies that are due by Saturday may squeeze out INR500 billion from banks, Swain estimated, while a federal government bond auction Friday will drain another INR70 billion from the banking system.   \par \par \uc2 Banks are the biggest buyers of sovereign debt and hence less cash with them affects demand for securities, putting pressure on prices.   \par \par \uc2 Swain said he expects the 10-year yield to trade in a band of 7.85%-7.90% this week.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee weakened marginally against the U.S. dollar on dogged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market participants said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to INR39.41 from its close of INR39.39 Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "There was some talk of inflows from recent overseas share issues by Indian companies coming in, so the Reserve Bank of India must have bought heavily for the dollar to close higher," said the chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a large foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 The trader said he expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in a INR39.35-INR39.45 band in the coming session.   \par \par \uc2 -By Neelabh Chaturvedi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91-22-22884212-18; neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com [ 10-12-07 1254GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071210e3ca00162\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
