\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Gain As Liquidity Improves; Rupee Down   \b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2007\par 14:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.49      +0.07 \par  7.99% 2017 Bond   7.87%      Unchanged \par  Call Rate         7.25%      -60 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  November          0.44       +0.02 \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. .    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bonds rose Wednesday on the view that banks' spare will rise in coming days, boosting demand for debt, traders said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 A near-certain cut in its benchmark rate by the U.S. Federal Reserve Dec. 11 and increasing demand from provident funds and insurance companies for long-dated debt will likely help the market sustain its rally in the coming sessions, they said.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.99% 2017 bond ended at INR100.78, compared with INR100.73 at Tuesday's close. During the session, it rose to INR100.88 before being knocked off its peak by dealers' profit-taking.   \par \par \uc2 "There has been a good amount of buying in the longer end of the curve and its absolute attractiveness remains intact," said Mahendra Jajoo, head of fixed income and structured products at  \uc2 ABN Amro Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 Jajoo said the yield spread between the 10- and 15-year bonds will narrow further in the coming days as insurance players will continue to buy more long-dated bonds.   \par \par \uc2 Yields on the bonds due in 2022 have fallen by nearly 15 basis points in the last week on heavy buying by provident funds and insurance firms.   \par \par \uc2 The most actively traded 8.20% 2022 bond ended at INR101.20, up from INR100.90 at the previous close.   \par \par \uc2 "The market also feels that demand from provident funds will increase this month as they usually redeploy their dividend and interest earnings in December," said an official at a primary dealership which underwrites sovereign bond auctions.   \par \par \uc2 He said banking system liquidity is expected to improve due to the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Banks are the largest buyers of sovereign debt in India and an increase in their excess cash spurs demand for bonds.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee weakened against the U.S. dollar Wednesday amid suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR39.49, up from INR39.42 at Tuesday's close.   \par \par \uc2 "State-run banks were buying dollars towards the end of the session and it looks like they were buying for the RBI," said a private bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to trade in a narrow range in the coming sessions, with the RBI likely to absorb foreign fund inflows to prevent any sharp gains of the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 -By Vipin V. Nair; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; 34.nair@dowjones.com [ 05-12-07 1310GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071205e3c5000oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
